4. Experimental Protocol

4.1 Datasets and Constraints

· METR-LA: 207 sensors, speed. Constraint: bounded acceleration and fundamental diagram.
· PEMS-BAY: 325 sensors, flow and occupancy. Constraint: flow conservation.
· NREL-AL: 137 solar sensors. Constraint: bounded temporal variation.
· Chicago Network: Scalability testing.
· Synthetic: Linear-Gaussian toy + controlled graph topologies.

4.2 Evaluation Regimes (Leakage-Free)

1. Geographically separated targets (primary). Target sensors spatially disjoint from training and validation.
2. Temporally separated targets. Target period disjoint from training and validation.
3. Spatio-temporally separated. Both space and time disjoint.
4. Genuinely new graph configurations. Test structural generalization.

Critical fix from v3.0: Bounds are computed from training nodes only. Validation and test nodes are never used in the LP, eliminating the leakage identified in the v3.0 review.

4.3 Baselines

· Spatial interpolation (KNN, IDW)
· IGNNK (Wu et al., 2021)
· FUNS (Roth & Liebig, 2022)
· MoGERNN (Zhou et al., 2025)
· SC-SAMG (Wang et al., 2026)
· GenST (Li et al., 2026)
· DRIK (Yang et al., 2026)
· Conformal Inductive GNN (Zargarbashi & Bojchevski, 2024)
· GP kriging variance

4.4 Metrics

· Point accuracy: MAE, RMSE
· Probabilistic accuracy: CRPS, NLL
· Calibration: Coverage, ECE, sharpness
· Partial identification: Bound width W(d), normalized width W_{\text{norm}}, coverage within Imbens–Manski confidence intervals
· OOD robustness: Test-to-validation MAE ratio (DRIK metric)
· Decision value: Expected decision loss, minimax regret, VoI, profiled regret

4.5 Ablations

· Remove semantic metadata
· Remove graph edges
· Remove probabilistic modeling
· Remove active selection
· Replace semantic embeddings with coordinates and distances
· Remove each DRIK mechanism (SCR, MFD, SDE)
· Remove LLM contamination controls
· Vary \varepsilon in A2 to test error propagation

