D.4 Graph Construction

The adjacency matrix for traffic datasets is constructed based on geographic proximity: the closer a pair of nodes, the more likely they are connected. Geodesic distances on Earth between nodes are computed and normalized; distances smaller than a threshold are chosen as edges . The threshold is chosen through an experiment designed in Li et al. (2017). For METR-LA, the graph has 1,722 edges and 207 nodes, with an average degree of approximately 16.6.

