Appendix I: Imbens–Manski Confidence Interval Construction

I.1 Standard IM Interval

For a partially identified parameter with identification region [\mu_-, \mu_+], the IM confidence interval is

CI_\alpha = \left[ \hat{\mu}_- - c_\alpha \frac{\hat{\sigma}_{\mu_-}}{\sqrt{n}}, \quad \hat{\mu}_+ + c_\alpha \frac{\hat{\sigma}_{\mu_+}}{\sqrt{n}} \right],

where c_\alpha is chosen such that

\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P}(\mu \in CI_\alpha) = 1 - \alpha

for all \mu \in [\mu_-, \mu_+] .

I.2 Uniform Coverage Modification

The simplest version of the IM CI does not converge uniformly across different values for the width of the identification region. The modified CI ensures uniform convergence .

I.3 Implementation in Algorithm C.3

In Algorithm C.3, the IM CI is computed from the estimated bounds \hat{\mu}_- and \hat{\mu}_+ and their standard errors \hat{\sigma}_{\mu_-} and \hat{\sigma}_{\mu_+}, estimated by bootstrap over the training data.

